# Backend (Python)

Managed with **[Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/)** — `pyproject.toml` + `poetry.lock` are the source of truth.

| Concern | Choice |
|--------|--------|
| Runtime | Python ≥ 3.10 |
| API | FastAPI + Pydantic |
| Tests | pytest (+ pytest-asyncio for async routes) |
| CLI | Rich |
| Jobs | JSON metadata + logs on disk under `NEUROFLOW_DATA_ROOT` |

## Structure & quality

- Packages by concern: `api/`, `services/`, `tools/`, `models/`.
- Type hints on public APIs; long jobs return immediately with `job_id` — never block HTTP on compute.
- Subprocess: allowlisted executables only, no `shell=True`, argv built from Pydantic models.
- `poetry add` + commit lockfile; run via `poetry run`.

## REST API

- Resources: `health`, `tools`, per-tool `jobs` and `log`.
- Prefix: `/api/v1/`; consistent errors (`detail`, `code`, optional `field`).
- OpenAPI is the contract for frontend and integrators.
